# tests/expected-t14-fidelity.golden -- R111.M7-026 (paideia-os #2378)
#
# Ordered-substring fingerprint contract for tools/run-qemu-t14fidelity.sh.
# Each non-blank, non-comment line must appear as a substring of the
# serial log, in the order listed, before the smoke declares PASS.
#
# All four lines are single-source-of-truth pins for real-HW-path
# fingerprints that earlier T14 waves landed but that no default -kernel
# QEMU smoke can exercise (each is currently in
# tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh's UEFI-only allowlist).  When
# this smoke starts running in CI, those allowlist entries retire in
# favor of this golden.
#
# Order rationale:
#   1. UEFI EBS OK           -- fires from the UEFI stub finalizer just
#                               before the higher-half kernel jump.
#   2. UEFI BRIDGE OK        -- fires from kernel_main_uefi Phase 5,
#                               immediately before call kernel_main_64.
#   3. UEFI PML4 OK          -- fires from uefi_bootstrap_pml4_install,
#                               after the mov cr3, rax that swaps in the
#                               PVH-shape identity + higher-half PML4.
#   4. ACPI RSDP HANDOFF OK  -- fires from kernel_main_64's
#                               phase1_emit_rsdp_fingerprint (line 1 of
#                               the R20 witness).
#   5. FB CONSOLE OK         -- fires from gop_fb_console_init, right
#                               after phase1_emit_rsdp_fingerprint.
#   6. SHELL START           -- src/user/shell.pdx L20; the shell-prompt
#                               witness (also the tier-1 anchor the
#                               script uses to break out of the wait
#                               loop).
#
UEFI EBS OK
UEFI BRIDGE OK
UEFI PML4 OK
ACPI RSDP HANDOFF OK
FB CONSOLE OK
SHELL START
